### Differences Between Java and TypeScript

| Feature                | Java                                          | TypeScript                                   |
|------------------------|----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Syntax for classes     | `public class Car`                           | `class Car`                                 |
| Access modifiers       | `private`, `public`                         | `private`, `public`                         |
| Constructor syntax     | `public Car(...)`                            | `constructor(...)`                           |
| Type declarations      | `int year;`                                 | `year: number;`                            |
| Exception handling      | `throw new IllegalArgumentException(...)`  | `throw new Error(...)`                      |
| String interpolation    | `+` operator for concatenation               | Template literals with `${}`                |

